<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- The entitlements a DISTRIBUTED build is signed with. Used by
	     scripts/package-macos.sh; hyperwave.entitlements is the local
	     development pair, and the difference between them is the point.

	     What must NOT be here, and is why this file exists at all:
	     com.apple.security.get-task-allow, which lets a debugger attach.
	     Apple's notary service refuses outright to notarize anything
	     carrying it, and it says so only in a log that has to be fetched
	     separately by submission id — so the failure arrives as
	     "status: Invalid" with no reason attached. That is what v0.1.0's
	     first tag cost. com.apple.security.cs.debugger is the same class of
	     thing and is likewise absent.

	     Not sandboxed. System audio capture via CoreAudio process taps is
	     gated by a TCC grant (kTCCServiceAudioCapture), not by an
	     entitlement, and it is not clear taps are permitted under App Sandbox
	     at all. Sandboxing would buy nothing and might cost the one feature
	     this app has.

	     apple-events exists for Sparkle. A hardened-runtime app has to be
	     allowed to relaunch itself after the updater swaps the binary, and
	     that relaunch is an Apple Event to itself. Without it the update
	     installs and the app never comes back, which looks like the update
	     broke it.

	     audio-input is what lets "Include microphone input" hear the
	     built-in microphone. The hardened runtime refuses the built-in mic to
	     any app without it, and refuses it silently: no prompt, no error, an
	     IO proc that runs and delivers zeros. USB mics and interfaces are not
	     gated the same way, so v0.2.0 worked with those and heard nothing
	     from a MacBook's own mic. Local builds are not hardened and never
	     showed it. package-macos.sh refuses to sign without this key. -->
	<key>com.apple.security.automation.apple-events</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
